`k=v` and `k!=v` partition the same vault: the two runs return disjoint sets whose union is
every plan, so the `!` suffix reaches the engine as a negated clause rather than as part of
the field name.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/alpha/index.md --
---
title: Alpha
status: ready-for-dev
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/beta/index.md --
---
title: Beta
status: done
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/gamma/index.md --
---
title: Gamma
status: done
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where status=done --output paths
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where 'status!=done' --output paths
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/beta/index.md
plans/gamma/index.md
plans/alpha/index.md
